# Plan: Improve DebugControls Icons and Tooltips

## Summary
Replace custom SVG icons in DebugControls with Lucide React icons (VS Code-style) and add Radix UI tooltips for better UX.

## Current State
- **File**: `lira-playground/frontend/src/components/Header/DebugControls.tsx`
- **Icons**: 6 custom inline SVG components (PlayIcon, PauseIcon, StepIntoIcon, StepOverIcon, StepOutIcon, ResetIcon)
- **Tooltips**: Native HTML `title` attributes (browser default, delayed, unstyled)

## Changes

### 1. Install Dependencies
```bash
cd lira-playground/frontend
pnpm add lucide-react @radix-ui/react-tooltip
```

### 2. Update DebugControls.tsx

**Replace icon imports** - Use Lucide icons that match VS Code debug toolbar:
| Action | Lucide Icon |
|--------|-------------|
| Continue | `Play` |
| Pause | `Pause` |
| Step Into | `ArrowDownToLine` |
| Step Over | `ArrowRightToLine` |
| Step Out | `ArrowUpFromLine` |
| Stop/Reset | `Square` (stop) or `RotateCcw` (reset) |

**Add Radix Tooltip wrapper** - Create a reusable `IconButton` component with tooltip:
```tsx
import * as Tooltip from '@radix-ui/react-tooltip';

function IconButton({ icon: Icon, label, shortcut, ...props }) {
  return (
    <Tooltip.Root>
      <Tooltip.Trigger asChild>
        <button className="icon-button" {...props}>
          <Icon size={16} />
        </button>
      </Tooltip.Trigger>
      <Tooltip.Portal>
        <Tooltip.Content className="tooltip-content" sideOffset={5}>
          {label}
          {shortcut && <span className="tooltip-shortcut">{shortcut}</span>}
          <Tooltip.Arrow className="tooltip-arrow" />
        </Tooltip.Content>
      </Tooltip.Portal>
    </Tooltip.Root>
  );
}
```

**Wrap component with Tooltip.Provider**

### 3. Update DebugControls.css

Add tooltip styles:
```css
.tooltip-content {
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  padding: 6px 10px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  font-size: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  z-index: 1000;
}

.tooltip-shortcut {
  color: var(--text-tertiary);
  font-size: 11px;
  background: var(--bg-secondary);
  padding: 2px 6px;
  border-radius: 3px;
}

.tooltip-arrow {
  fill: var(--bg-elevated);
}
```

### 4. Delete Inline SVG Components
Remove the 6 custom icon function components (PlayIcon, PauseIcon, etc.) - no longer needed.

## Files to Modify
1. `lira-playground/frontend/package.json` - Add dependencies
2. `lira-playground/frontend/src/components/Header/DebugControls.tsx` - Replace icons and add tooltips
3. `lira-playground/frontend/src/components/Header/DebugControls.css` - Add tooltip styles

## Expected Result
- Recognizable VS Code-style debug icons
- Instant, styled tooltips with keyboard shortcuts displayed
- Accessible (Radix handles ARIA, focus, keyboard navigation)
- ~10KB bundle size increase (lucide tree-shakes, radix is minimal)

# Fuzzy File Finder Implementation Plan

## Overview
Add `Cmd+Shift+O` fuzzy file finder to quickly search and open files in the current workspace.

- **`Cmd+O`**: Unchanged - opens native file picker
- **`Cmd+Shift+O`**: NEW - fuzzy file finder modal (replaces old "Open Folder" binding)

Uses `nucleo` crate for fast fuzzy matching.
Respects existing ignore patterns (`.git`, `node_modules`, `target/`, etc.).

---

## Files to Modify

| File | Changes |
|------|---------|
| `Cargo.toml` | Add `nucleo` dependency |
| `src/model/ui.rs` | Add `ModalId::FileFinder`, `FileFinderState`, `FileMatch` |
| `src/keymap/command.rs` | Replace `OpenFolder` with `FuzzyFileFinder` command |
| `keymap.yaml` | Change `cmd+shift+o` from `OpenFolder` → `FuzzyFileFinder` |
| `src/model/workspace.rs` | Add `FileTree::get_all_file_paths()` method |
| `src/update/ui.rs` | Handle fuzzy finder modal messages |
| `src/view/mod.rs` | Render file finder modal |
| `src/messages.rs` | Add `UiMsg::OpenFuzzyFileFinder` |

---

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Add `nucleo` Dependency (`Cargo.toml`)
```toml
[dependencies]
nucleo = "0.5"
```

### Step 2: Add Modal State Types (`src/model/ui.rs`)

Add to `ModalId` enum:
```rust
/// File finder (Cmd+Shift+O) - fuzzy search files in workspace
FileFinder,
```

Add new structs:
```rust
/// A file match result from fuzzy search
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub struct FileMatch {
    pub path: PathBuf,
    pub filename: String,        // Just the file name
    pub relative_path: String,   // Path from workspace root
    pub score: u32,              // Fuzzy match score (higher = better)
    pub indices: Vec<u32>,       // Character indices that matched (for highlighting)
}

/// State for the file finder modal
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub struct FileFinderState {
    pub editable: EditableState<StringBuffer>,
    pub selected_index: usize,
    pub results: Vec<FileMatch>,
    pub all_files: Vec<PathBuf>,  // Cached file list
}
```

Add to `ModalState` enum:
```rust
FileFinder(FileFinderState),
```

Update `ModalState::id()`:
```rust
ModalState::FileFinder(_) => ModalId::FileFinder,
```

### Step 3: Add File Collection (`src/model/workspace.rs`)

Add method to `FileTree`:
```rust
/// Get all file paths recursively (excludes directories)
pub fn get_all_file_paths(&self) -> Vec<PathBuf> {
    let mut files = Vec::new();
    for root in &self.roots {
        Self::collect_files_recursive(root, &mut files);
    }
    files
}

fn collect_files_recursive(node: &FileNode, files: &mut Vec<PathBuf>) {
    if node.is_dir {
        for child in &node.children {
            Self::collect_files_recursive(child, files);
        }
    } else {
        files.push(node.path.clone());
    }
}
```

### Step 4: Update Command (`src/keymap/command.rs`)

Replace `OpenFolder` with `FuzzyFileFinder`:
```rust
/// Fuzzy file finder - search workspace files (Cmd+Shift+O)
FuzzyFileFinder,
```

In `to_msgs()`:
```rust
FuzzyFileFinder => vec![Msg::Ui(UiMsg::OpenFuzzyFileFinder)],
```

### Step 5: Update Keybinding (`keymap.yaml`)

```yaml
- key: "cmd+shift+o"
  command: FuzzyFileFinder  # Changed from OpenFolder
```

### Step 6: Add Message Types (`src/messages.rs`)

Add to `UiMsg`:
```rust
/// Open fuzzy file finder modal
OpenFuzzyFileFinder,
```

### Step 7: Update Handlers

**A) Handle `UiMsg::OpenFuzzyFileFinder`** (`src/update/ui.rs`):
```rust
UiMsg::OpenFuzzyFileFinder => {
    if model.workspace.is_none() {
        model.ui.set_status("No workspace open");
        return Some(Cmd::Redraw);
    }
    let all_files = model.workspace.as_ref()
        .map(|w| w.file_tree.get_all_file_paths())
        .unwrap_or_default();
    let state = FileFinderState::new(all_files);
    model.ui.open_modal(ModalState::FileFinder(state));
    Some(Cmd::Redraw)
}
```

**B) Update `ToggleModal` handler** to include `ModalId::FileFinder`:
```rust
ModalId::FileFinder => {
    let all_files = model.workspace.as_ref()
        .map(|w| w.file_tree.get_all_file_paths())
        .unwrap_or_default();
    ModalState::FileFinder(FileFinderState::new(all_files))
}
```

**C) Add match arms in `update_modal()`** for `ModalMsg` variants:
- `InsertChar` → insert char, re-filter results, reset selected_index
- `DeleteBackward` → delete char, re-filter results
- `SelectNext` / `SelectPrevious` → navigate results list
- `Confirm` → open selected file via `LayoutMsg::OpenFileInNewTab(path)`
- Cursor movement variants → delegate to `state.editable`

**D) Remove OpenFolder references**:
- Remove `OpenFolder` command from `src/keymap/command.rs`
- Remove `OpenFolderDialog` message handling (or keep for programmatic use)
- Remove `cmd+shift+o` → `OpenFolder` from `keymap.yaml`

### Step 8: Implement Fuzzy Matching

Create helper function (in `src/update/ui.rs` or new `src/fuzzy.rs`):
```rust
use nucleo::{Matcher, Config, Utf32String};

pub fn fuzzy_match_files(
    files: &[PathBuf],
    query: &str,
    workspace_root: &Path
) -> Vec<FileMatch> {
    if query.is_empty() {
        // Show all files sorted alphabetically when no query
        return files.iter()
            .take(100)  // Limit initial display
            .map(|p| FileMatch::from_path(p, workspace_root, 0, vec![]))
            .collect();
    }

    let mut matcher = Matcher::new(Config::DEFAULT);
    let mut results: Vec<_> = files.iter()
        .filter_map(|path| {
            let filename = path.file_name()?.to_str()?;
            let mut indices = Vec::new();
            let score = matcher.fuzzy_indices(
                &Utf32String::from(filename),
                &Utf32String::from(query),
                &mut indices
            )?;
            Some(FileMatch::from_path(path, workspace_root, score, indices))
        })
        .collect();

    // Sort by score descending
    results.sort_by(|a, b| b.score.cmp(&a.score));
    results.truncate(50);  // Limit results
    results
}
```

### Step 9: Render Modal (`src/view/mod.rs`)

Add case in `render_modals()`:
```rust
ModalState::FileFinder(state) => {
    // Modal dimensions (centered, 600px wide)
    let (modal_x, modal_y, modal_width, modal_height) =
        geometry::modal_bounds(window_width, window_height, 600, 400);

    // Background
    frame.draw_bordered_rect(modal_x, modal_y, modal_width, modal_height, ...);

    // Title: "Go to File"
    painter.draw(frame, title_x, title_y, "Go to File", fg_color);

    // Input field
    TextFieldRenderer::render(frame, painter, &state.editable, &text_field_opts);

    // Results list
    let max_visible = 10;
    for (i, file_match) in state.results.iter().take(max_visible).enumerate() {
        let is_selected = i == state.selected_index;
        let row_y = results_start_y + (i as f32 * row_height);

        // Selection highlight
        if is_selected {
            frame.fill_rect(modal_x, row_y, modal_width, row_height, selection_bg);
        }

        // File icon
        let icon = FileExtension::from_path(&file_match.path).icon();
        painter.draw(frame, icon_x, row_y, icon, icon_color);

        // Filename (with match highlighting)
        painter.draw(frame, name_x, row_y, &file_match.filename, fg_color);

        // Relative path (dimmed)
        painter.draw(frame, path_x, row_y, &file_match.relative_path, dim_color);
    }
}
```

---

## Behavior Summary

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `Cmd+O` | Opens native file picker (unchanged) |
| `Cmd+Shift+O` | Opens fuzzy file finder modal |

### Fuzzy File Finder (`Cmd+Shift+O`)
| Scenario | Action |
|----------|--------|
| With workspace | Opens fuzzy finder modal |
| Without workspace | Shows "No workspace open" status message |
| Type in finder | Filters files by fuzzy match |
| Arrow Up/Down | Navigate results |
| Enter | Open selected file in new tab |
| Escape | Close modal |

---

## Testing

1. **Unit test**: Fuzzy matching algorithm correctness
2. **Integration test**: Modal opens/closes properly
3. **Integration test**: File opens on confirm
4. **Manual test**: Performance with large workspace (1000+ files)

# Plan: Server-Side Filtering & Sorting

## Problem

Currently filtering/sorting happens client-side on only loaded plans. With lazy loading (100 plans at a time), searching for "glados" only searches within loaded plans, missing results that haven't been fetched yet.

## Solution

Pass search, sort, and project filter params to the API. Server returns filtered/sorted results with proper pagination.

---

## API Changes

### `/api/plans` endpoint (updated)

**New query params:**
- `q` - search query (searches title, content, filename, project)
- `sort` - sort key: `modified|created|title|project|size|lines`
- `dir` - sort direction: `asc|desc`
- `projects` - comma-separated project names to filter by

**Example:**
```
GET /api/plans?offset=0&limit=50&q=glados&sort=modified&dir=desc&projects=project1,project2
```

### `/api/projects` endpoint (new)

**Response:**
```ts
{ projects: string[] }  // All unique project names, sorted alphabetically
```

---

## Files to Modify

### 1. `index.ts` (Backend)

Update `/api/plans` route handler:
```ts
// Parse new params
const q = url.searchParams.get("q")?.toLowerCase() || "";
const sort = url.searchParams.get("sort") || "modified";
const dir = url.searchParams.get("dir") || "desc";
const projectsParam = url.searchParams.get("projects");
const projectFilter = projectsParam ? new Set(projectsParam.split(",")) : null;

// Filter plans
let filtered = allPlans.filter(plan => {
  // Project filter
  if (projectFilter && (!plan.project || !projectFilter.has(plan.project))) {
    return false;
  }
  // Search filter
  if (q) {
    return plan.title.toLowerCase().includes(q) ||
           plan.content.toLowerCase().includes(q) ||
           plan.filename.toLowerCase().includes(q) ||
           (plan.project?.toLowerCase().includes(q) ?? false);
  }
  return true;
});

// Sort plans
filtered.sort((a, b) => { /* sort logic */ });

// Paginate
const paginated = filtered.slice(offset, offset + limit);
```

### 2. `src/client/hooks/usePlans.ts`

Add filter params to fetch:
```ts
interface FetchParams {
  offset: number;
  limit: number;
  q?: string;
  sort?: SortKey;
  dir?: SortDir;
  projects?: string[];
}

async function fetchPlans(params: FetchParams) {
  const url = new URL("/api/plans", window.location.origin);
  url.searchParams.set("offset", String(params.offset));
  url.searchParams.set("limit", String(params.limit));
  if (params.q) url.searchParams.set("q", params.q);
  if (params.sort) url.searchParams.set("sort", params.sort);
  if (params.dir) url.searchParams.set("dir", params.dir);
  if (params.projects?.length) {
    url.searchParams.set("projects", params.projects.join(","));
  }
  // ... fetch
}
```

### 3. `src/client/hooks/useFilters.ts`

Remove client-side filtering logic. This hook becomes a simple state container that triggers refetches when filters change.

### 4. `src/client/App.tsx`

Connect filter state to usePlans:
```ts
const { searchQuery, sortKey, sortDir, selectedProjects } = useFilters();
const { plans, total, loading, loadMore, refresh } = usePlans({
  q: searchQuery,
  sort: sortKey,
  dir: sortDir,
  projects: Array.from(selectedProjects),
});
```

---

## Key Considerations

1. **Debounce search** - Don't hit API on every keystroke. Debounce 300ms.

2. **Reset offset on filter change** - When search/sort/filter changes, reset to offset 0.

3. **Abort previous requests** - Cancel in-flight requests when filters change.

4. **Keep content in cache** - Plan content should persist across filter changes.

5. **Projects list** - Separate `/api/projects` endpoint for dropdown.

---

## Implementation Order

1. Backend: Add `/api/projects` endpoint
2. Backend: Update `/api/plans` to accept and process filter/sort params
3. Frontend: Update `usePlans` hook to pass params to API
4. Frontend: Add `useProjects` hook to fetch project list
5. Frontend: Simplify `useFilters` to just manage state (no client-side filtering)
6. Frontend: Connect everything in App.tsx
7. Frontend: Add debouncing for search input
8. Test with e2e tests

# Glyph Cache Cleanup Plan

## Summary

Remove dead glyph cache helper methods from `src/view/mod.rs`.

## Dead Code to Remove

| Method | Lines | Reason for Removal |
|--------|-------|--------|
| `glyph_cache_mut()` | 146-149 | Zero callers - external cache access never used |
| `get_char_width()` | 2275-2286 | Superseded by pre-calculated `self.char_width` field |

## Context

The glyph cache is properly used through `TextPainter` with direct field access:
```rust
let mut painter = TextPainter::new(&self.font, &mut self.glyph_cache, font_size, ascent);
```

The helper methods served no purpose:
- `glyph_cache_mut()` - Would allow external mutation, but nothing calls it
- `get_char_width()` - Memoization is redundant since `char_width` is computed once at init (line 97-98)

## File to Modify

`src/view/mod.rs`

## Implementation Steps

1. Remove `glyph_cache_mut()` method (lines 146-149):
   ```rust
   #[allow(dead_code)]
   pub fn glyph_cache_mut(&mut self) -> &mut GlyphCache {
       &mut self.glyph_cache
   }
   ```

2. Remove `get_char_width()` method (lines 2275-2286):
   ```rust
   #[allow(dead_code)]
   fn get_char_width(&mut self) -> f32 {
       let key = ('m', self.font_size.to_bits());
       if let Some((metrics, _)) = self.glyph_cache.get(&key) {
           metrics.advance_width
       } else {
           let (metrics, bitmap) = self.font.rasterize('m', self.font_size);
           let width = metrics.advance_width;
           self.glyph_cache.insert(key, (metrics, bitmap));
           width
       }
   }
   ```

3. Run `make lint` to verify no new warnings
4. Run `make test` to ensure nothing breaks

# Damage Tracking Implementation Plan

## Overview

Implement partial redraw optimization to avoid full-frame rendering on every update. Currently, **all 208 redraw triggers** cause full window redraws, including cursor blink (2Hz) which alone accounts for ~50% of idle redraws.

## Key Design Decisions

### Damage Granularity: 3 levels

```rust
pub enum DamageArea {
    EditorArea,              // All groups + tab bars + gutters + text + splitters
    StatusBar,               // Bottom status line only
    CursorLines(Vec<usize>), // Specific lines for cursor blink optimization
}

pub enum Damage {
    Full,                    // Redraw everything (safe fallback)
    Areas(Vec<DamageArea>),  // Partial redraw
}
```

**Rationale:**
- EditorArea + StatusBar for coarse operations
- CursorLines for fine-grained cursor blink optimization (biggest win)
- Per-group tracking deferred to follow-up task

### Correctness Principle

When in doubt, fall back to `Damage::Full`. Force full redraw for:
- Modal overlays active (dim background accumulation)
- Debug overlays visible
- Window resize
- Theme changes
- Layout changes (splits)

---

## Implementation Phases

### Phase 1: Add Types (30 min)
**File:** `src/commands.rs`

1. Add `Damage` enum and `DamageArea` enum
2. Add `Cmd::RedrawAreas(Vec<DamageArea>)` variant
3. Implement `Cmd::damage() -> Damage` method
4. Update `Cmd::needs_redraw()` to handle new variant

### Phase 2: Renderer Signature (30 min)
**Files:** `src/view/mod.rs`, `src/runtime/app.rs`

1. Change `Renderer::render()` to accept `damage: &Damage` parameter
2. Pass `Damage::Full` everywhere initially (no behavior change)
3. Store pending damage in `App` struct

### Phase 3: Coarse Partial Render (1 hour)
**File:** `src/view/mod.rs`

1. Compute effective damage (force Full for modals/overlays)
2. Implement conditional clear for EditorArea vs StatusBar
3. Skip rendering undamaged regions

### Phase 4: Cursor-Line Optimization (1-2 hours)
**Files:** `src/view/mod.rs`, `src/model/ui.rs`, `src/update/ui.rs`

1. Track previous cursor lines in `UiState`:
   ```rust
   pub struct UiState {
       // ... existing fields
       pub previous_cursor_lines: Vec<usize>,  // Lines that had cursors last frame
   }
   ```

2. In cursor blink handler, compute dirty lines:
   - Current cursor lines (from `editor.cursors`)
   - Previous cursor lines (from `ui.previous_cursor_lines`)
   - Union = lines to redraw

3. Return `Cmd::RedrawAreas(vec![CursorLines(dirty_lines)])` instead of `Cmd::Redraw`

4. In renderer, for `CursorLines(lines)`:
   - Only clear and redraw the specified line rectangles
   - Include gutter area for those lines (current line indicator)
   - Include current line highlight background

### Phase 5: Wire Up Update Functions (1 hour)
**Files:** `src/update/*.rs`

Convert appropriate `Cmd::Redraw` calls to `Cmd::RedrawAreas`:

| Operation | Damage |
|-----------|--------|
| **Cursor blink** | `CursorLines(dirty_lines)` |
| Cursor movement | `EditorArea` |
| Text editing | `EditorArea` |
| Selection changes | `EditorArea` |
| Scrolling | `EditorArea` |
| Status text change | `StatusBar` |
| Tab dirty indicator | `EditorArea + StatusBar` |
| Modal open/close | Keep `Cmd::Redraw` (Full) |
| Theme/resize/layout | Keep `Cmd::Redraw` (Full) |

### Phase 6: Debug Visualization (30 min, compile-time flag)
**Files:** `src/view/mod.rs`, `Cargo.toml`

1. Add feature flag `damage-debug` in Cargo.toml
2. When enabled, draw colored rectangles around damage regions:
   - Red outline for EditorArea
   - Blue outline for StatusBar
   - Green outline for CursorLines

### Phase 7: Testing & Validation (1 hour)
1. Visual artifact testing (no stale pixels)
2. Benchmark partial vs full render times
3. Test cursor blink with damage-debug enabled

---

## Critical Files to Modify

```
src/commands.rs          - Add Damage/DamageArea types and Cmd::RedrawAreas variant
src/view/mod.rs          - Partial render logic, cursor-line rendering
src/runtime/app.rs       - Store pending damage, pass to renderer
src/model/ui.rs          - Add previous_cursor_lines tracking
src/update/ui.rs         - Cursor blink returns CursorLines damage
src/update/editor.rs     - Cursor movement returns EditorArea damage
src/update/document.rs   - Text editing returns EditorArea damage
Cargo.toml               - Add damage-debug feature flag
```

---

## Data Structures

```rust
// src/commands.rs

#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum DamageArea {
    /// All editor groups, tab bars, gutters, text areas, splitters
    EditorArea,
    /// Bottom status bar only
    StatusBar,
    /// Specific lines for cursor blink (line numbers are document-relative)
    CursorLines(Vec<usize>),
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default)]
pub enum Damage {
    /// Redraw everything (always safe fallback)
    #[default]
    Full,
    /// Redraw specific areas only
    Areas(Vec<DamageArea>),
}

impl Damage {
    /// Merge another damage into this one
    pub fn merge(&mut self, other: Damage) {
        match (self, other) {
            (Damage::Full, _) => {} // Already full, nothing to do
            (this, Damage::Full) => *this = Damage::Full,
            (Damage::Areas(areas), Damage::Areas(other_areas)) => {
                for area in other_areas {
                    // Merge CursorLines specially (combine line lists)
                    if let DamageArea::CursorLines(lines) = &area {
                        if let Some(existing) = areas.iter_mut().find_map(|a| {
                            if let DamageArea::CursorLines(l) = a { Some(l) } else { None }
                        }) {
                            for line in lines {
                                if !existing.contains(line) {
                                    existing.push(*line);
                                }
                            }
                            continue;
                        }
                    }
                    // For EditorArea/StatusBar, just add if not present
                    if !areas.contains(&area) {
                        areas.push(area);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    /// Check if this damage includes the editor area
    pub fn includes_editor(&self) -> bool {
        match self {
            Damage::Full => true,
            Damage::Areas(areas) => areas.iter().any(|a| matches!(a, DamageArea::EditorArea)),
        }
    }
}
```

```rust
// src/model/ui.rs - Addition to UiState

pub struct UiState {
    // ... existing fields ...

    /// Lines that contained cursors in the previous frame (for damage tracking)
    /// Updated by renderer after drawing cursors
    pub previous_cursor_lines: Vec<usize>,
}
```

---

## Render Logic Pseudocode

```rust
pub fn render(&mut self, model: &mut AppModel, damage: &Damage) -> Result<()> {
    // Force full for complex overlays
    let effective = if model.ui.active_modal.is_some()
        || model.debug_overlay.is_some() {
        Damage::Full
    } else {
        damage.clone()
    };

    match &effective {
        Damage::Full => {
            frame.clear(bg_color);
            self.render_editor_area(...);
            self.render_status_bar(...);
        }
        Damage::Areas(areas) => {
            // Handle cursor-line-only damage (most common case for blink)
            let cursor_lines: Option<&Vec<usize>> = areas.iter().find_map(|a| {
                if let DamageArea::CursorLines(lines) = a { Some(lines) } else { None }
            });

            if let Some(lines) = cursor_lines {
                // Only redraw specific lines (cursor blink optimization)
                self.render_cursor_lines_only(&mut frame, model, lines);
            } else {
                // Coarse damage areas
                if areas.iter().any(|a| matches!(a, DamageArea::EditorArea)) {
                    frame.fill_rect(editor_rect, bg_color);
                    self.render_editor_area(...);
                }
                if areas.iter().any(|a| matches!(a, DamageArea::StatusBar)) {
                    frame.fill_rect(status_rect, status_bg);
                    self.render_status_bar(...);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // Update previous cursor lines for next frame's damage calculation
    model.ui.previous_cursor_lines = self.collect_current_cursor_lines(model);

    // Modals always on top (only rendered with Full damage)
    if model.ui.active_modal.is_some() {
        self.render_modals(...);
    }

    // Debug: show damage regions
    #[cfg(feature = "damage-debug")]
    self.render_damage_debug(&mut frame, &effective);
}

/// Render only the specified lines (for cursor blink)
fn render_cursor_lines_only(&self, frame: &mut Frame, model: &AppModel, lines: &[usize]) {
    for &line in lines {
        // Calculate line rect (gutter + text area for this line)
        let line_rect = self.compute_line_rect(model, line);

        // Clear line background
        frame.fill_rect(line_rect, bg_color);

        // Render current line highlight if this is the cursor line
        if line == model.editor().active_cursor().line {
            frame.fill_rect(line_rect, current_line_bg);
        }

        // Render line number in gutter
        self.render_line_number(frame, model, line);

        // Render text content for this line
        self.render_line_text(frame, model, line);

        // Render cursor if visible and on this line
        if model.ui.cursor_visible {
            self.render_cursors_on_line(frame, model, line);
        }
    }
}
```

