pub enum PageFaultResult {
    Handled,
    GrowStack,
    GrowHeap,
    CopyOnWrite,
    AccessViolation,
    InvalidAddress,
    OutOfMemory,  // NEW: Allocation failed
}
```

Kernel handler treats `OutOfMemory` as SIGKILL (unrecoverable).

#### 2.3 TLB Invalidation

Document when `invlpg` is required:
- After COW copy: `invlpg` on modified page
- After demand page: Not needed (page was not present)
- After stack growth: `invlpg` on each newly mapped page
- After munmap: `invlpg` on unmapped pages

#### 2.4 Concurrent Fault Handling

```rust
pub fn handle_page_fault(...) -> PageFaultResult {
    // Lock process memory for duration of fault handling
    let memory = process.memory.lock();

    // Re-check if page is now present (another thread may have mapped it)
    if memory.address_space.is_present(fault_addr) {
        return PageFaultResult::Handled;  // Race resolved
    }

    // ... rest of handler
}
```

